ISSUES - known issues of snd-usb-mytek 2.2

1 - No ALSA card after switching the Mytek on
    The firmware is uploaded in three stages, with a USB disconnect and
    reconnect after each. Right after power-on an upload stage can fail
    ("unable to upload fpga firmware", probe error -32). Reload the module:

        sudo modprobe -r snd_usb_mytek && sudo modprobe snd_usb_mytek

    scripts/mytekusb2-firmware-loader.sh retries this automatically.
    Also check the kernel log for missing firmware files (see FIRMWARE).

2 - "Pre-initialised Mytek with missing FPGA firmware, please cycle its
    power" / "invalid firmware version in device"
    The DAC was initialised by another computer or driver version. Switch
    the Mytek off and on again.

3 - Clicks when DSD starts or stops
    The DAC clicks when it switches between PCM and DSD: often when a DSD
    stream starts, and at the end of every DSD128 stream (the display then
    shows "no lock" until the next stream). Consecutive tracks of the same
    DSD rate played gaplessly do not switch. The driver already keeps
    these to a minimum (dop_preroll, dop_exit, see README.md); the rest
    happens inside the DAC. PCM rate changes do not click (unmute_delay).

4 - The display shows 88.2 or 176.4 for a moment after DSD
    After a DSD stream the driver sends dop_exit ms of PCM silence at the
    DoP carrier rate (352.8k or 176.4k) so the DAC leaves DSD mode; the
    DAC displays that briefly. Cosmetic.

5 - No volume control
    The DAC has no USB-controllable volume. Use the DAC's own volume or
    the player's software volume.

6 - PCM above 192 kHz
    The DAC plays PCM up to 192 kHz; the driver offers nothing higher.
    352.8 kHz is used only as the DoP carrier for DSD128 (see dop352 in
    README.md for players that make DoP themselves).
